  "ghost": {
   "spec": "SPEC 4: < 2% of ghost-mask pixels deviate by > 0.5 EV from the reference",
   "definition": "Bedroom (3 hand-held TIFF frames, moving object). GT = radiance_capture.tif with the object drawn at the reference frame's position (synthetic.moving_object, as generated), in reference-frame geometry. Ghost mask = union of the object's footprints (blurred mask > 0.5) of all frames. The series is loaded, aligned and merged by the pipeline at full resolution (2400x1600); the radiance scale is normalised by the median log2 luminance ratio merged/GT over unclipped pixels outside the ghost mask (dilated 15 px) and outside windows. Deviation = max over R,G,B of |log2(merged_c / GT_c)| after that scale: the object (navy) is about as bright as what it covers, so a transparent trace is mainly a colour shift (frac_dev_gt_0.5ev_luminance = the same with luminance only, much less sensitive). Reported: fraction of ghost-mask pixels deviating > 0.5 EV (also split by the object's reference position / the other frames' positions, and the rate on non-ghost pixels = noise floor of the metric); pixels saturated in GT even in the darkest frame or with the merge's clipped map >= 0.01 are excluded (excluded_clipped_px). deghost_off = the same merge with deghost.enabled=false (shows that the metric detects ghosts).",
